/-!
# The Cotlar--Stein almost orthogonality lemma

Let `T i`, `i ∈ s`, be a finite family of bounded operators between Hilbert spaces.  If the
"column sums" `∑ k, ‖(T i)* ∘ T k‖ ^ (1/2)` and the "row sums" `∑ k, ‖T i ∘ (T k)*‖ ^ (1/2)`
are both bounded by `A`, then `‖∑ i, T i‖ ≤ A`.

This is the classical almost orthogonality lemma of Cotlar, Knapp and Stein.  The proof
formalized here is the standard one: one expands `‖∑ T i‖ ^ (2 n)` as `‖((∑ T i)* (∑ T i)) ^ n‖`,
expands the `n`-th power into a sum over alternating words

`(T i₁)* (T j₁) (T i₂)* (T j₂) ⋯ (T iₙ)* (T jₙ)`,

bounds each word by the geometric mean of the two groupings

`∏ ‖(T iₗ)* (T jₗ)‖`  and  `‖T i₁‖ ⬝ ∏ ‖(T jₗ) (T iₗ₊₁)*‖ ⬝ ‖T jₙ‖`,

sums the resulting alternating chain of square roots one index at a time, and lets `n → ∞`
along the powers of two.

## Main result

* `Auto.CotlarStein.norm_sum_le_of_cotlar_stein`

## References

* M. Cotlar, *A combinatorial inequality and its applications to L²-spaces*,
  Rev. Mat. Cuyana **1** (1955), 41–55.
* E. M. Stein, *Harmonic analysis*, Ch. VII, §2.
-/

